module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.Evaluation

/-!
# The derived evaluation functor and its unit

Let `C` be a differential graded category over a commutative ring `R`, let `K` be an object of
`C` and let `G` be a family of objects of `C`. Step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] produced, in
`DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory`, an exact
reflector `L : K(Mod^dg(C)) ⥤ K(Mod^dg(C))` onto the objects right orthogonal to the
localizing subcategory `N` generated by the representables `h_{G i}`, together with a unit
`η : 𝟭 ⟶ L` whose cones lie in `N`. Evaluation at `K` of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.Evaluation` is exact, so the
composite

`R̃ = L ⋙ ev_K : K(Mod^dg(C)) ⥤ K(Mod^dg(C(K, K)))`

is an exact functor to the homotopy category of right differential graded `C(K, K)`-modules,
and `ev_K η` is a natural transformation `ev_K ⟶ R̃`. Whiskering it with the differential
graded Yoneda functor gives a natural transformation `Hom(K, -) ⟶ R̃ ∘ h` out of the functor
`X ↦ C(K, X)` of [Stacks, Tag 09LE]: this is the transformation step 2 of the argument
asks the localization unit to supply.

## What is and is not composed with the step-1 embedding

The step-1 functor `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaVerdierEmbedding` is
`J : A/(A ⊓ N) ⥤ K(Mod^dg(C))/N`, a functor between Verdier quotients. Evaluation at `K` does
*not* descend to `K(Mod^dg(C))/N`: a representable `h_X` evaluates to the complex `C(K, X)`,
which is not in general zero or acyclic, so `ev_K` does not invert the morphisms whose cone
lies in `N`, and the literal composite `ev_K ∘ J` is not available. What takes its place is
the reflector: `L` sends an object to its universal map into an `N`-local object, which is the
derived-functor value that the quotient computes, and `R̃ = L ⋙ ev_K` is the exact
`Mod^dg(C(K, K))`-valued functor step 2 of the argument names. The two agree on the local
objects, where `η` is an isomorphism.

## Main definitions

* `DGCategory.evaluationReflectorUnit`: the natural transformation `ev_K ⟶ L ⋙ ev_K` obtained
  by applying `ev_K` to a unit `η : 𝟭 ⟶ L`.
* `DGCategory.homDGReflectorUnit`: its restriction along the differential graded Yoneda
  functor, a natural transformation `Hom(K, -) ⟶ h ⋙ L ⋙ ev_K`.

## Main results

* `DGCategory.exists_isTriangulated_evaluationReflector`: step 2 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] for the
  reflector of step 1 — the reflector together with the exactness of `R̃ = L ⋙ ev_K` and the
  natural transformation `ev_K ⟶ R̃` supplied by its unit.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DGCategory

universe v u r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R] (C : DGCategory.{v, u} R) (K : C.Obj)

/-- **The unit of the derived evaluation functor.** Applying evaluation at `K` to a natural
transformation `η : 𝟭 ⟶ L` gives a natural transformation `ev_K ⟶ L ⋙ ev_K`, whose component
at `M` is `ev_K` of the component of `η`. -/
def evaluationReflectorUnit
    (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L) :
    evaluationOnK.{v} C K ⟶ L ⋙ evaluationOnK.{v} C K :=
  Functor.whiskerRight η (evaluationOnK.{v} C K)

/-- The component of `evaluationReflectorUnit C K L η` at `M` is `ev_K` applied to `η.app M`. -/
@[simp] theorem evaluationReflectorUnit_app
    (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L)
    (M : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) :
    (evaluationReflectorUnit C K L η).app M = (evaluationOnK.{v} C K).map (η.app M) := rfl

/-- **The transformation `Hom(K, -) ⟶ R̃ ∘ h`.** The unit of the derived evaluation functor,
restricted along the differential graded Yoneda functor `X ↦ h_X`: its source is the functor
`X ↦ C(K, X)` of [Stacks, Tag 09LE], read on the homotopy category. -/
def homDGReflectorUnit
    (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L) :
    (yonedaDGFunctor C).onK ⋙ evaluationOnK.{v} C K ⟶
      (yonedaDGFunctor C).onK ⋙ (L ⋙ evaluationOnK.{v} C K) :=
  Functor.whiskerLeft (yonedaDGFunctor C).onK (evaluationReflectorUnit C K L η)

/-- The component of `homDGReflectorUnit C K L η` at `X` is `ev_K` applied to the component of
`η` at the representable `h_X`. -/
@[simp] theorem homDGReflectorUnit_app
    (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L)
    (X : C.K) :
    (homDGReflectorUnit C K L η).app X =
      (evaluationOnK.{v} C K).map (η.app ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK.obj X)) := rfl

/-- **Step 2 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK], for the reflector of step 1.** Let `C` be a differential
graded category whose objects and whose morphism modules live in one universe, let `K` be an
object of `C` and let `G` be a family of objects of `C` indexed by that universe. Then the
exact reflector `L` and unit `η : 𝟭 ⟶ L` of step 1
(`DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory`) satisfy in
addition:

* `R̃ = L ⋙ ev_K`, with values in the homotopy category of right differential graded modules
  over the endomorphism complex `E = C(K, K)` of `K`, is exact;
* `ev_K η` is a natural transformation `ev_K ⟶ R̃`.

Both are consequences of the exactness of evaluation at `K`,
`DGCategory.isTriangulated_evaluationOnK`. The values of `R̃` carry their `E`-action because
they are evaluations of right differential graded `C`-modules at `K`
(`DGCategory.evaluation_obj_act`), and `E` is the endomorphism complex `C(K, K)` of `C`
itself. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_evaluationReflector (C : DGCategory.{v, v} R) (K : C.Obj)
    {ι : Type v} (G : ι → C.Obj) :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L),
      (∀ X, (ofObj fun i => RightModule.yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.rightOrthogonal
          (L.obj X)) ∧
      (∀ Y, (ofObj fun i =>
            RightModule.yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.rightOrthogonal Y →
        ∀ X, Function.Bijective fun φ : L.obj X ⟶ Y => η.app X ≫ φ) ∧
      (∀ (X Z) (f : Z ⟶ X) (g : L.obj X ⟶ Z⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
        Triangle.mk f (η.app X) g ∈ distTriang _ →
          (ofObj fun i => RightModule.yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v} Z) ∧
      (L ⋙ evaluationOnK.{v} C K).IsTriangulated ∧
      ∀ M, (evaluationReflectorUnit C K L η).app M =
        (evaluationOnK.{v} C K).map (η.app M) := by
  obtain ⟨L, cs, tri, η, h₁, h₂, h₃⟩ :=
    RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory C G
  have := cs
  have := tri
  have := isTriangulated_evaluationOnK.{v} C K
  exact ⟨L, cs, tri, η, h₁, h₂, h₃, inferInstance, fun _ => rfl⟩

end DGCategory
